<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  DriveAppStorageService (LaunchAgent) entitlements.

  Not sandboxed, hardened runtime ON (project-wide ENABLE_HARDENED_RUNTIME), no
  com.apple.security.cs.* exceptions. Why not sandboxed for B01:
  - launchd starts it from the app bundle via SMAppService; it publishes the Mach service named in
    its LaunchAgent plist. Keeping the sandbox out of the spike removes one variable from the G0
    question "is the published Mach service reachable from the sandboxed app and FSKit extension".
  - B01 reads no user files, Keychain items or network; it serves an in-memory fixture catalog.
  - Before B02 adds tokens, cache and the database, record an ADR on sandboxing this agent
    (docs/04-architecture.md: never broaden access merely to bypass a failed setup).

  App Group: the same group as the app and the extension. The Mach service name is prefixed by it,
  and later builds will share the group container (staging/cache) with the app.
  G0-VERIFY: a command-line tool cannot embed a provisioning profile; TEAMID-prefixed macOS app
  groups do not need one, but confirm AMFI accepts this entitlement on the signed tool.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>$(DEVELOPMENT_TEAM).$(APP_BUNDLE_ID)</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
